How It Works:

This project lets users generate likeability scores of athletes. It uses a sentiment-analysis model that we trained on the sentiment140 dataset from Kaggle. Using a reddit api we got reddit comments and filtered to ensure they contained the athlete's name. We then passed those comments through the model to generate positive or negative predictions. The athlete's oerall "favorability score" is computed as the percentage of comments classified as positive. These results are stored ina JSON file and siplayed through a Flask web inteface.

How to Use It

To run the flask app run the visualize.py file. This will open up in a url to access the dashboard. The page will automatically load three athletes that we tested the model on. This is to speed up the process as you don't have to wait a minute to see initial data. You can add your own athlete by typing there name into the search bar and clicking "Add". The system will automatically add them to the dashboard (It may take up to one minute, but is usually faster). We initially created this application to get sentiment for athletes, but we realized it can be used on anything or anyone.
